  "lineage": "Early-1990s Norwegian heavy-metal subgenre developed from broader 1980s first-wave black-metal (Venom, Bathory, Hellhammer) into a distinct Norwegian extreme-metal style. Characterized by tremolo-picked-guitar-blast-beat percussion, raw-and-lo-fi production aesthetic, screeched-or-shrieked vocal-delivery, and explicit Norse-pagan-and-Satanic thematic content. Mayhem (founded 1984), Burzum, Darkthrone, Emperor, Immortal, and the broader Norwegian black-metal scene anchored the canonical aesthetic. The early-1990s church-arson and murder controversies mythologized the scene.",
